From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] serial: qcom-geni: power the SE down in system suspend

Since the runtime PM conversion, qcom_geni_serial_pm() turns a port off
with pm_runtime_put_sync(). In system suspend it is reached from
uart_suspend_port() while the PM core still holds the runtime PM reference
it took in device_prepare(), so the put never suspends the device: the SE
clock (and with it the GCC PLL and the XO vote), its OPP and its ICC vote
stay on through s2idle. On the ROG Phone 5 the console and Bluetooth UARTs
were the last XO users at the moment the SoC went to sleep, and the AOSS
never entered CXSD/AOSS sleep.

Force the runtime suspend after uart_suspend_port() turned the port off,
and force the resume before uart_resume_port(). A port that stays on as a
wakeup source is left powered.

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c	2026-09-28 02:53:28.980055586 +0200
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c	2026-09-28 02:53:47.174405417 +0200
@@ -1983,6 +1983,7 @@
 	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct uart_port *uport = &port->uport;
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
+	int ret;
 
 	/*
 	 * This is done so we can hit the lowest possible state in suspend
@@ -1992,7 +1993,22 @@
 		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY);
 		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
 	}
-	return uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	ret = uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * uart_suspend_port() releases the port with pm_runtime_put_sync(),
+	 * but the PM core holds a runtime PM reference across system suspend
+	 * (device_prepare()), so the SE clock, its OPP and ICC votes stayed on
+	 * and kept XO voted: the SoC never reached CXSD/AOSS sleep (ROG5
+	 * console and Bluetooth UARTs). Power the SE down here instead, unless
+	 * the port stayed on as a wakeup source.
+	 */
+	if (uport->state && uport->state->pm_state == UART_PM_STATE_ON)
+		return 0;
+
+	return pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
 }
 
 static int qcom_geni_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
@@ -2002,6 +2018,10 @@
 	struct uart_port *uport = &port->uport;
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
 
+	ret = pm_runtime_force_resume(dev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	ret = uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
 	if (uart_console(uport)) {
 		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS);
